      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/topup/quote?credits=100",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "topup",
            "quote"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "credits",
              "value": "100",
              "description": "Number of credits to price."
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Price a credit top-up before paying for it. No authentication. Credits cost $0.02 each; the minimum is 25 credits ($0.50, the card minimum) and the maximum is 50,000 per call.",
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Buy Credits (machine payment)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"status is one of 200\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200]));",
              "pm.test(\"response is JSON\", () => pm.response.to.be.json);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "<authorization>",
            "description": "The payment credential, sent by the MPP client on the retried request after paying one of the challenges from the 402. Absent on the first request.",
            "disabled": true
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/topup",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "topup"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Buy credits for the account owning the API key, paid by the caller itself over the Machine Payments Protocol (MPP, https://mpp.dev). No checkout page and no card form.\n\nThe first call answers 402 Payment Required with a WWW-Authenticate header carrying two Payment challenges, one for USDC on Tempo (method \"tempo\") and one for card or Link via a Stripe shared payment token (method \"stripe\"). The client pays one of them and repeats the same request with the payment credential; any MPP client (mppx, the Stripe Link CLI) does this automatically. The repeated request answers 200 and the credits are on the balance at once.\n\nRules: $0.02 per credit, minimum 25 credits, maximum 50,000 per call. Card top-ups are capped at $100 per account per rolling 24 hours; over the cap the 402 offers USDC only, which is uncapped. A trial account moves to the Starter pay-as-you-go price table on its first top-up and no subscription is created. A payment credential never credits twice: a replay answers 200 with status \"already_credited\".\n\nPay from the command line with a USDC wallet (npx -y mppx@0.9.2 https://api.myotp.app/v1/topup -X POST -H \"x-api-key: KEY\" -H \"content-type: application/json\" -d '{\"credits\":100}') or with a Link agent wallet (npx -y @stripe/link-cli mpp pay https://api.myotp.app/v1/topup -X POST -d '{\"credits\":100}' -H \"x-api-key: KEY\" --context \"MyOTP credits\").",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"credits\": 100\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Create an account (agent signup)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"status is one of 201\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([201]));",
              "pm.test(\"response is JSON\", () => pm.response.to.be.json);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/agent/register",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "agent",
            "register"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Create a MyOTP.App account without a browser. No authentication. The 201 body carries the API key exactly once; store it and send it as X-API-Key on every later request.\n\nRules: no trial credits and no phone verification. The balance starts at zero, so the account can send nothing until it is topped up with POST /v1/topup. USDC top-ups work immediately; card top-ups are offered only after the account email is confirmed. The IP allowlist is open (\"*\") for agent accounts. Five registrations per IP address per 24 hours. The human signup at https://myotp.app/sign-up is unchanged: 15 free credits, email and phone verification.\n\nEmail confirmation: the address receives \"Confirm your MyOTP.App account email\" from raya@myotp.app with a link to /v1/agent/verify-email. A human has to open it and press Confirm; the agent cannot confirm on the user's behalf. The link is single use and valid for 24 hours.\n\nAgent flow: register, save the api_key, tell the human to click the email link (optional, only needed for cards), GET /v1/topup/quote, POST /v1/topup and pay the 402 (USDC works without the email step), then POST /generate_otp as usual. A 403 \"Insufficient balance\" on any send means: top up again.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"dev@example.com\",\n  \"name\": \"Acme\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "auth": {
          "type": "noauth"
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
